{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Implement a Levenshtein distance approximation for short strings: given two text values, compute the edit distance by building a row-by-row dynamic programming table stored as a list of lists."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```falcon\nfunc levenshtein(s1, s2) =\n  {\n    local dp = []\n    for (i: 0 .. s1.textLen() step 1) {\n      local row = []\n      for (j: 0 .. s2.textLen() step 1) {\n        row.add(0)\n      }\n      dp.add(row)\n    }\n    for (i: 1 .. s1.textLen() + 1 step 1) {\n      dp[i][1] = i - 1\n    }\n    for (j: 1 .. s2.textLen() + 1 step 1) {\n      dp[1][j] = j - 1\n    }\n    for (i: 2 .. s1.textLen() + 1 step 1) {\n      for (j: 2 .. s2.textLen() + 1 step 1) {\n        local cost = if (s1.segment(i - 1, 1) === s2.segment(j - 1, 1)) {\n          0\n        } else {\n          1\n        }\n        local del = dp[i - 1][j] + 1\n        local ins = dp[i][j - 1] + 1\n        local sub = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + cost\n        dp[i][j] = min(del, min(ins, sub))\n      }\n    }\n    dp[s1.textLen() + 1][s2.textLen() + 1]\n  }\n```"}]}
