{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Write `kmpSearch(text, pattern)` \u2014 KMP string search: return all 1-based starting positions. Test `(\"ababcabab\",\"abab\")` \u2192 `[1,6]`."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```falcon\nfunc kmpSearch(text, pattern) =\n  {\n    local n = text.textLen()\n    local m = pattern.textLen()\n    local lps = []\n    for (i: 1 .. m step 1) {\n      lps.add(0)\n    }\n    local len = 0\n    local i = 2\n    while (i <= m) {\n      if (pattern.segment(i, 1) === pattern.segment(len + 1, 1)) {\n        len = len + 1\n        lps[i] = len\n        i = i + 1\n      } else if (len > 0) {\n        len = lps[len]\n      } else {\n        lps[i] = 0\n        i = i + 1\n      }\n    }\n    local result = []\n    local j = 1\n    i = 1\n    while (i <= n) {\n      if (text.segment(i, 1) === pattern.segment(j, 1)) {\n        i = i + 1\n        j = j + 1\n      }\n      if (j > m) {\n        result.add(i - m)\n        j = lps[j - 1] + 1\n      } else if (i <= n && text.segment(i, 1) !== pattern.segment(j, 1)) {\n        if (j > 1) {\n          j = lps[j - 1] + 1\n        } else {\n          i = i + 1\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    result\n  }\n\nprintln(kmpSearch(\"ababcabab\", \"abab\"))\n```"}]}
